[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128430,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 232,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Epithelioid fibrous histiocytoma (EFH) is a distinctive, usually exophytic and well-circumscribed benign cutaneous neoplasm composed of epithelioid cells, including binucleated forms. <em>ALK</em> rearrangement is present in the vast majority of cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T15:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128431,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 232,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8830/0 Epithelioid fibrous histiocytoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T15:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128432,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 232,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E85.2 &amp; XH15M9 Benign fibrohistiocytic tumour of skin &amp; Epithelioid fibrous histiocytoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T15:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128433,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 232,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Acceptable:</em> epithelioid cell histiocytoma.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-06-30T10:35:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128434,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 232,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T15:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128435,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 232,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EFH most commonly affects the lower extremities, followed by the upper extremities. The trunk and the head and neck region are uncommon sites {7909998; 10027517; 2466472; 8181804}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T15:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128436,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 232,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EFH manifests as an exophytic nodule, often with a vascular appearance {2466472}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T15:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128437,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 232,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EFH typically arises in young to middle-aged adults (median age: 40&nbsp;years), with a female predominance {7909998; 2466472; 8181804}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T15:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128438,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 232,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T15:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128439,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 232,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Although the histogenesis is unknown, EFH is probably biologically distinct from dermatofibroma (conventional fibrous histiocytoma) and its subtypes {26763770; 25857825}. EFHs harbour rearrangements of <em>ALK</em> (in ~90% of cases) or a PRKC gene (rarely), as mutually exclusive events {25857825; 24666231; 26121314}. <em>SQSTM1</em> and <em>VCL</em> are the most common <em>ALK</em> fusion partners; rare fusions partners are <em>DCTN1</em>, <em>ETV6</em>, <em>PPFIBP1</em>, <em>SPECC1L</em>, <em>TPM3</em>, <em>PRKAR2A</em>, <em>MLPH</em>, <em>CLTC</em>, and <em>EML4</em> {25413595; 29327718; 29329131; 35289445}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T15:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128440,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 232,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients typically present with a well-circumscribed dermal papule.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T15:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128441,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 232,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EFH is usually well circumscribed; exophytic examples often have an adnexal collarette. The tumour is composed of uniform plump epithelioid cells with vesicular nuclei, small nucleoli, and abundant pale eosinophilic or amphophilic cytoplasm, often including binucleated forms. Small, thin-walled blood vessels may be prominent, sometimes with perivascular accentuation of tumour cells. Chondroblastoma-like pericellular calcification {29068085; 34086645} and lesions mostly composed of spindle cells {29430713; 33217002} have been described. ALK is overexpressed in about 90% of cases {25857825}, with higher positivity with the D5F3 or 5A4 clones than with the ALK1 clone {25857825; 34929229}, and EMA is positive in 65% {21752057}. CD30 expression may be seen {25857825; 24666231}. CD31, SMA, and desmin are usually negative {21752057; 25596243}.</p>\r\n<h6>Differential diagnosis</h6>\r\n<p>The differential diagnosis includes Spitz naevus, cutaneous syncytial myoepithelioma, epithelioid sarcoma, and cellular neurothekeoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T15:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128442,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 232,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T15:04:05"
      }
    ],
